1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,254
A pickup that cost two hundred eighty-one

2
00:00:03,254 --> 00:00:03,889
dollars.

3
00:00:04,069 --> 00:00:06,716
A truck that was legally turned into

4
00:00:06,716 --> 00:00:08,995
a car by bolting two seats into

5
00:00:08,995 --> 00:00:09,584
its bed.

6
00:00:09,764 --> 00:00:12,239
A trade war over chicken that still

7
00:00:12,239 --> 00:00:14,714
decides which trucks you can buy in

8
00:00:14,714 --> 00:00:15,987
twenty twenty-six.

9
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:18,600
And a small hybrid pickup that Ford

10
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,799
sold more than one hundred fifty-five thousand

11
00:00:21,799 --> 00:00:22,912
times last year.

12
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:25,847
These are the pickups that changed America,

13
00:00:25,847 --> 00:00:28,025
and most people only know half the

14
00:00:28,025 --> 00:00:28,409
story.

15
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,362
Each one of these trucks changed something

16
00:00:31,362 --> 00:00:33,160
bigger than the truck market.

17
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:34,626
How Americans work,

18
00:00:34,626 --> 00:00:35,708
where they live,

19
00:00:35,708 --> 00:00:36,656
what they pay,

20
00:00:36,656 --> 00:00:38,889
and even the laws of the country.

21
00:00:39,069 --> 00:00:41,023
And every one of them still shapes

22
00:00:41,023 --> 00:00:42,862
the truck you will buy in twenty

23
00:00:42,862 --> 00:00:43,609
twenty-seven.

24
00:00:43,789 --> 00:00:45,962
Some of the twists in this story

25
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:48,270
are so strange they sound made up.

26
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:49,089
They are not.

27
00:00:49,269 --> 00:00:51,393
Every one of them is documented.

28
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:54,211
Every number in this video comes from

29
00:00:54,211 --> 00:00:55,478
a published source,

30
00:00:55,478 --> 00:00:57,212
listed in the description.

31
00:00:57,392 --> 00:00:59,435
If we could not confirm a figure,

32
00:00:59,435 --> 00:01:00,364
we left it out.

33
00:01:00,544 --> 00:01:03,266
Let's go back almost exactly one hundred

34
00:01:03,266 --> 00:01:05,647
years, to the truck that started it

35
00:01:05,647 --> 00:01:05,919
all.

36
00:01:06,269 --> 00:01:09,423
Number one is the nineteen twenty-five Ford

37
00:01:09,423 --> 00:01:12,063
Model T Runabout with a pickup body.

38
00:01:12,243 --> 00:01:14,824
According to The Henry Ford museum,

39
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:18,291
Ford introduced its light-duty Model T runabout

40
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:21,020
pickup in April nineteen twenty-five.

41
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,175
It came with a factory-installed steel pickup

42
00:01:24,175 --> 00:01:24,439
bed.

43
00:01:24,619 --> 00:01:26,666
And it was priced at two hundred

44
00:01:26,666 --> 00:01:27,882
eighty-one dollars.

45
00:01:28,231 --> 00:01:31,037
Before this, if you wanted a pickup,

46
00:01:31,037 --> 00:01:33,297
you usually bought a car or a

47
00:01:33,297 --> 00:01:35,636
chassis and had a bed built by

48
00:01:35,636 --> 00:01:36,649
someone else.

49
00:01:36,829 --> 00:01:39,487
Farmers cut the back off their cars.

50
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:42,895
Small companies sold conversion kits.

51
00:01:43,075 --> 00:01:44,570
Ford's idea was simple:

52
00:01:44,570 --> 00:01:46,584
build the truck at the factory,

53
00:01:46,584 --> 00:01:48,014
sell it at the dealer,

54
00:01:48,014 --> 00:01:50,288
and make it cheap enough for anyone

55
00:01:50,288 --> 00:01:52,108
who worked with their hands.

56
00:01:52,457 --> 00:01:53,073
It worked.

57
00:01:53,253 --> 00:01:54,942
According to The Henry Ford,

58
00:01:54,942 --> 00:01:58,019
the company sold nearly thirty-three thousand eight

59
00:01:58,019 --> 00:02:00,010
hundred units in that first year.

60
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:02,419
For a brand-new kind of vehicle,

61
00:02:02,419 --> 00:02:04,021
that was a huge number.

62
00:02:04,201 --> 00:02:07,754
Farmers, delivery workers and small business owners

63
00:02:07,754 --> 00:02:10,261
suddenly had a tool that could carry

64
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:12,142
goods to town and back in a

65
00:02:12,142 --> 00:02:12,909
single day.

66
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,779
And here is the twist.

67
00:02:14,959 --> 00:02:17,466
The Model T pickup was not designed

68
00:02:17,466 --> 00:02:19,615
as a lifestyle vehicle at all.

69
00:02:19,795 --> 00:02:20,851
It was a tool.

70
00:02:21,031 --> 00:02:22,911
But it planted an idea in the

71
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:25,438
American mind that has never gone away:

72
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:27,447
that a working person can own a

73
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:29,845
vehicle that does real work and still

74
00:02:29,845 --> 00:02:31,724
drive it to church on Sunday.

75
00:02:31,904 --> 00:02:33,630
Every pickup sold today,

76
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:36,865
from a work truck to a ninety-thousand-dollar

77
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:39,381
luxury model, comes from that idea.

78
00:02:39,731 --> 00:02:42,242
The Model T pickup also changed where

79
00:02:42,242 --> 00:02:43,667
Americans could live.

80
00:02:43,847 --> 00:02:46,171
A farmer with a truck could live

81
00:02:46,171 --> 00:02:49,002
farther from town and still sell crops.

82
00:02:49,182 --> 00:02:51,666
A builder could carry tools to jobs

83
00:02:51,666 --> 00:02:52,944
across the county.

84
00:02:53,124 --> 00:02:56,700
Small towns grew around roads instead of

85
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,594
railroads.

86
00:02:57,774 --> 00:03:00,006
The pickup became part of how rural

87
00:03:00,006 --> 00:03:02,494
America worked, long before it became a

88
00:03:02,494 --> 00:03:03,834
symbol on television.

89
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:05,553
Think about the price.

90
00:03:05,733 --> 00:03:09,321
Two hundred eighty-one dollars in nineteen twenty-five.

91
00:03:09,501 --> 00:03:13,027
Today, the average new full-size pickup costs

92
00:03:13,027 --> 00:03:16,162
many times what the average worker earns

93
00:03:16,162 --> 00:03:17,024
in a month.

94
00:03:17,204 --> 00:03:19,624
The Model T pickup was affordable by

95
00:03:19,624 --> 00:03:20,095
design.

96
00:03:20,275 --> 00:03:21,802
That idea, the cheap,

97
00:03:21,802 --> 00:03:23,694
simple truck for everyone,

98
00:03:23,694 --> 00:03:26,676
is exactly what disappeared over the next

99
00:03:26,676 --> 00:03:27,694
hundred years.

100
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:29,840
And it is exactly what the last

101
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,934
truck on this list tried to bring

102
00:03:31,934 --> 00:03:32,251
back.

103
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,541
Number two is a truck that was

104
00:03:34,541 --> 00:03:35,770
not really a truck.

105
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:37,605
In nineteen fifty-seven,

106
00:03:37,605 --> 00:03:39,468
Ford launched the Ranchero.

107
00:03:39,648 --> 00:03:40,560
It was a car,

108
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,734
with the front of a Ford sedan,

109
00:03:42,734 --> 00:03:44,908
and a pickup bed where the back

110
00:03:44,908 --> 00:03:46,591
seat and trunk would be.

111
00:03:46,771 --> 00:03:47,885
Two years later,

112
00:03:47,885 --> 00:03:50,532
Chevrolet answered with the El Camino.

113
00:03:50,712 --> 00:03:53,121
A new kind of vehicle was born:

114
00:03:53,121 --> 00:03:54,753
the car-based pickup.

115
00:03:55,102 --> 00:03:56,182
Why did it matter?

116
00:03:56,362 --> 00:03:58,486
Because it was the first time an

117
00:03:58,486 --> 00:04:01,208
American carmaker openly sold a pickup as

118
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:02,469
a lifestyle choice.

119
00:04:02,649 --> 00:04:05,687
The Ranchero and El Camino rode like

120
00:04:05,687 --> 00:04:07,628
cars, looked like cars,

121
00:04:07,628 --> 00:04:09,822
and came with car engines,

122
00:04:09,822 --> 00:04:11,763
including big V eights.

123
00:04:11,943 --> 00:04:14,169
They were for people who wanted the

124
00:04:14,169 --> 00:04:16,459
image and the usefulness of a truck,

125
00:04:16,459 --> 00:04:17,922
without the rough ride.

126
00:04:18,271 --> 00:04:20,535
The El Camino became a legend.

127
00:04:20,715 --> 00:04:23,705
Chevrolet offered it with muscle car engines

128
00:04:23,705 --> 00:04:26,424
in the late sixties and early seventies,

129
00:04:26,424 --> 00:04:29,821
and today the high-performance versions are prized

130
00:04:29,821 --> 00:04:30,433
classics.

131
00:04:30,613 --> 00:04:33,875
The Ranchero ended in nineteen seventy-nine.

132
00:04:34,055 --> 00:04:37,689
The El Camino lasted until nineteen eighty-seven.

133
00:04:37,869 --> 00:04:39,648
And then, for decades,

134
00:04:39,648 --> 00:04:42,397
the idea disappeared from America.

135
00:04:42,747 --> 00:04:44,152
Here is the twist.

136
00:04:44,332 --> 00:04:45,563
The idea did not die.

137
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:47,310
It just took a different form.

138
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:50,659
When Ford launched the small Maverick pickup

139
00:04:50,659 --> 00:04:52,171
in twenty twenty-one,

140
00:04:52,171 --> 00:04:54,259
built on a car-like platform,

141
00:04:54,259 --> 00:04:56,851
and Hyundai launched the Santa Cruz,

142
00:04:56,851 --> 00:05:00,019
many reviewers compared them to the Ranchero

143
00:05:00,019 --> 00:05:01,028
and El Camino.

144
00:05:01,208 --> 00:05:05,001
A comfortable, car-based truck for people who

145
00:05:05,001 --> 00:05:07,361
mostly drive on paved roads.

146
00:05:07,541 --> 00:05:11,188
The fifties idea came back sixty-five years

147
00:05:11,188 --> 00:05:11,697
later.

148
00:05:12,047 --> 00:05:14,494
There is another twist in the Ranchero

149
00:05:14,494 --> 00:05:14,880
story.

150
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:17,285
Ford launched the Ranchero first,

151
00:05:17,285 --> 00:05:19,511
but the El Camino became the more

152
00:05:19,511 --> 00:05:20,320
famous name.

153
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,415
Being first is not the same as

154
00:05:22,415 --> 00:05:22,926
winning.

155
00:05:23,106 --> 00:05:25,024
Chevrolet watched, waited,

156
00:05:25,024 --> 00:05:27,679
and then offered more power and more

157
00:05:27,679 --> 00:05:28,122
style.

158
00:05:28,302 --> 00:05:31,073
That pattern repeats again and again in

159
00:05:31,073 --> 00:05:32,423
the truck business,

160
00:05:32,423 --> 00:05:34,981
and it is still happening today with

161
00:05:34,981 --> 00:05:35,976
small pickups.

162
00:05:36,325 --> 00:05:39,054
And the Ranchero changed something deeper.

163
00:05:39,234 --> 00:05:41,587
It proved that many people who buy

164
00:05:41,587 --> 00:05:43,871
a pickup do not need a heavy-duty

165
00:05:43,871 --> 00:05:44,632
work truck.

166
00:05:44,812 --> 00:05:47,537
They want a bed for weekend projects,

167
00:05:47,537 --> 00:05:50,408
sports gear and home improvement trips.

168
00:05:50,588 --> 00:05:53,634
That insight is behind almost every pickup

169
00:05:53,634 --> 00:05:54,431
sold today.

170
00:05:54,611 --> 00:05:56,840
The modern pickup is as much a

171
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,772
family car as a work tool,

172
00:05:58,772 --> 00:06:01,224
and the Ranchero was the first to

173
00:06:01,224 --> 00:06:02,413
say so out loud.

174
00:06:02,763 --> 00:06:04,837
Number three is not one truck,

175
00:06:04,837 --> 00:06:07,257
but a law that changed every truck.

176
00:06:07,437 --> 00:06:08,981
And it started with chicken.

177
00:06:09,161 --> 00:06:11,322
According to The Daily Vroom,

178
00:06:11,322 --> 00:06:12,962
in nineteen sixty-two,

179
00:06:12,962 --> 00:06:16,837
European farmers objected to cheap American chicken,

180
00:06:16,837 --> 00:06:19,819
with West Germany leading the push back.

181
00:06:19,999 --> 00:06:22,530
Europe put tariffs on American chicken.

182
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:24,808
In nineteen sixty-four,

183
00:06:24,808 --> 00:06:30,192
President Lyndon Johnson responded with retaliatory tariffs

184
00:06:30,192 --> 00:06:32,474
on four European imports.

185
00:06:32,654 --> 00:06:34,662
One of them was light trucks.

186
00:06:35,012 --> 00:06:36,998
The rate was twenty-five percent.

187
00:06:37,178 --> 00:06:38,156
At the time,

188
00:06:38,156 --> 00:06:41,174
one of the targets was the Volkswagen

189
00:06:41,174 --> 00:06:43,701
pickup, based on the famous V W

190
00:06:43,701 --> 00:06:44,028
bus.

191
00:06:44,208 --> 00:06:47,579
Three of the four retaliatory tariffs were

192
00:06:47,579 --> 00:06:49,746
dropped within a few years.

193
00:06:49,926 --> 00:06:52,422
The tax on light trucks never was.

194
00:06:52,602 --> 00:06:55,215
As The Daily Vroom wrote in April

195
00:06:55,215 --> 00:06:58,461
twenty twenty-six, sixty-one years later,

196
00:06:58,461 --> 00:07:00,520
it is still sitting there.

197
00:07:00,869 --> 00:07:03,389
Think about how unusual that is.

198
00:07:03,569 --> 00:07:05,898
A trade dispute about poultry,

199
00:07:05,898 --> 00:07:09,315
between governments in the nineteen sixties,

200
00:07:09,315 --> 00:07:12,731
created a permanent rule for American pickup

201
00:07:12,731 --> 00:07:13,275
trucks.

202
00:07:13,455 --> 00:07:15,418
Most people who buy a truck today

203
00:07:15,418 --> 00:07:16,787
have never heard of it.

204
00:07:16,967 --> 00:07:19,567
Yet it quietly affects which brands sell

205
00:07:19,567 --> 00:07:21,776
trucks here, where they are built,

206
00:07:21,776 --> 00:07:23,271
and how much they cost.

207
00:07:23,621 --> 00:07:25,526
Here is where it gets strange.

208
00:07:25,706 --> 00:07:27,690
In the nineteen seventies,

209
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:31,429
small Japanese pickups became popular in America.

210
00:07:31,609 --> 00:07:34,197
To avoid the twenty-five percent tax,

211
00:07:34,197 --> 00:07:37,274
some companies shipped them without the bed,

212
00:07:37,274 --> 00:07:38,743
as a cab and chassis,

213
00:07:38,743 --> 00:07:40,491
which faced a lower rate.

214
00:07:40,671 --> 00:07:42,713
The beds were added after the trucks

215
00:07:42,713 --> 00:07:43,167
arrived.

216
00:07:43,347 --> 00:07:47,023
Chevrolet sold a small truck called the

217
00:07:47,023 --> 00:07:48,908
LUV, built by Isuzu.

218
00:07:49,088 --> 00:07:51,021
Ford sold the Courier,

219
00:07:51,021 --> 00:07:52,339
built by Mazda.

220
00:07:52,688 --> 00:07:55,054
And then came the craziest twist of

221
00:07:55,054 --> 00:07:55,324
all.

222
00:07:55,504 --> 00:07:59,335
Subaru sold a small car-based pickup called

223
00:07:59,335 --> 00:08:00,136
the BRAT.

224
00:08:00,316 --> 00:08:03,246
To avoid being classified as a light

225
00:08:03,246 --> 00:08:06,256
truck, it came with two plastic seats

226
00:08:06,256 --> 00:08:08,291
bolted into the open bed,

227
00:08:08,291 --> 00:08:09,674
facing backwards.

228
00:08:09,854 --> 00:08:12,308
With seats, the BRAT counted as a

229
00:08:12,308 --> 00:08:14,614
passenger vehicle, not a truck.

230
00:08:14,794 --> 00:08:16,893
Two seats in the back turned a

231
00:08:16,893 --> 00:08:18,153
pickup into a car,

232
00:08:18,153 --> 00:08:19,902
at least for the tax man.

233
00:08:20,252 --> 00:08:22,470
The loophole did not last forever.

234
00:08:22,650 --> 00:08:24,164
Rules were tightened,

235
00:08:24,164 --> 00:08:27,551
and over time Japanese companies began building

236
00:08:27,551 --> 00:08:29,929
pickups in North America instead.

237
00:08:30,109 --> 00:08:33,382
Today, Toyota builds its Tacoma and Tundra

238
00:08:33,382 --> 00:08:35,330
in North American plants,

239
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:38,214
and Nissan builds the Frontier in the

240
00:08:38,214 --> 00:08:39,305
United States.

241
00:08:39,485 --> 00:08:40,140
In a way,

242
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:43,269
the chicken tax pushed foreign truck makers

243
00:08:43,269 --> 00:08:45,452
to build factories in America.

244
00:08:45,802 --> 00:08:48,584
Why does a sixty-year-old chicken fight matter

245
00:08:48,584 --> 00:08:49,007
to you?

246
00:08:49,187 --> 00:08:51,512
Because the chicken tax is one of

247
00:08:51,512 --> 00:08:54,400
the reasons the American pickup market is

248
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,430
dominated by trucks built in North America.

249
00:08:57,610 --> 00:09:01,137
For decades, importing a pickup from Europe

250
00:09:01,137 --> 00:09:04,500
or Asia meant paying an extra twenty-five

251
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,156
percent.

252
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:08,711
That protected Detroit's most profitable vehicles,

253
00:09:08,711 --> 00:09:11,545
and it shaped which trucks Americans could

254
00:09:11,545 --> 00:09:11,815
buy.

255
00:09:12,164 --> 00:09:14,057
And here is the last twist.

256
00:09:14,237 --> 00:09:17,290
Many popular trucks from other countries,

257
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,928
like the Toyota Hilux,

258
00:09:18,928 --> 00:09:21,609
have never been sold new in America.

259
00:09:21,789 --> 00:09:23,787
And even if you try to import

260
00:09:23,787 --> 00:09:26,336
an old one under the twenty-five year

261
00:09:26,336 --> 00:09:28,885
rule, The Daily Vroom points out that

262
00:09:28,885 --> 00:09:31,365
the age exemption and the tariff are

263
00:09:31,365 --> 00:09:33,225
completely separate things.

264
00:09:33,405 --> 00:09:34,477
In its example,

265
00:09:34,477 --> 00:09:37,479
a nineteen ninety-four Hilux faced a three

266
00:09:37,479 --> 00:09:40,409
thousand nine hundred dollar tariff line,

267
00:09:40,409 --> 00:09:43,624
inside about eight thousand dollars in import

268
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:43,982
fees.

269
00:09:44,331 --> 00:09:46,579
So when people ask why small,

270
00:09:46,579 --> 00:09:49,602
cheap pickups disappeared from America,

271
00:09:49,602 --> 00:09:51,927
the chicken tax is part of the

272
00:09:51,927 --> 00:09:52,470
answer.

273
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:56,098
And in twenty twenty-five and twenty twenty-six,

274
00:09:56,098 --> 00:09:59,115
new tariffs on imported vehicles and parts

275
00:09:59,115 --> 00:10:01,485
added another layer on top of it.

276
00:10:01,665 --> 00:10:04,298
The chicken war of nineteen sixty-four is

277
00:10:04,298 --> 00:10:06,931
still deciding what is parked in American

278
00:10:06,931 --> 00:10:07,958
driveways today.

279
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:10,670
Number four is the truck that changed

280
00:10:10,670 --> 00:10:11,756
how pickups look.

281
00:10:11,936 --> 00:10:14,153
The nineteen ninety-four Dodge Ram.

282
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:17,664
